+## Why
+
+Services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is the published standard, and later features of this library will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to.
+- It throws an error when the pointer is not syntactically valid per RFC 6901, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Add the library's first source file and tests (`src/` does not exist yet).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: resolving RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code under `src/`; new public export `resolvePointer`. No dependencies added, no breaking changes.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment form (`#/a/b`), setting/removing values, and pointer construction.
